; bfsodium KECCAK RHO PI CHI : the second  third and fourth steps of a Keccak
; round  FIPS 202 section 3
;
; HAND WRITTEN; rho turns each lane left by its own fixed amount  pi sends each
; lane to a different place  and chi is the one non linear step  working along
; the rows; They are ONE file because the array pi writes is the array chi
; reads  so nothing between them is ever seen from outside;
;
; INTERFACE entry=200 exit=0 footprint=0:547
; IO  in:  A{200}  twenty five 64 bit lanes  each little endian
;     out: A{200}  the same  with rho  pi and chi applied
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x0c7  A{200}   the state  in AND out; lane k at cell 8k  where k is
;                          5y plus x for the lane FIPS 202 calls A{x y}
;   @0x0c8:0x0ed  the exclusive or frame; xor64 pasted at @0x0c8
;   @0x0ee:0x113  the and frame; and64 pasted at @0x0ee
;   @0x114:0x11b  T{8}     hands a lane back after it has been copied
;   @0x11c:0x143  W{40}    the work buffer; ONE ROW of B  brought down to sit
;                          beside the frames
;   @0x148:0x20f  B{200}   the state between pi and chi; lane k at 328 plus 8k
;   @0x210:0x223  the last rotation's frame  which reaches 27 cells past B{24}
;
; THE THREE STEPS  in FIPS 202's letters  every index modulo five:
;
;   B{y  2x plus 3y} = rotl(A{x y}  r{x y})        rho and pi together
;   A{x y} = B{x y} xor ((not B{x plus 1 y}) and B{x plus 2 y})           chi
;
; WHY THEY ARE ONE FILE AND NOT TWO  which is worth stating because the rest of
; this library splits things as far as it can: chi's input is B  and B lives
; high on the tape  so a chi of its own would have to READ two hundred bytes
; into cells three hundred and twenty eight upward; A read prologue may contain
; nothing but commas and steps and tools/bffoot refuses a routine whose prologue
; is preceded by any other command byte  for the good reason that a paste begins
; at the prologue and would silently drop whatever came before it; Joining the
; two steps removes the question: this file reads at nought  answers at nought
; and B is private to it;
;
; That also makes a round IN PLACE  which is the reason it matters rather than
; a tidiness: theta works on cells nought to 199 and so does this  so a round
; is two pastes at the same base and no state is ever carried between them;
;
; CHI USED TO FETCH EVERY OPERAND FROM B AND HAND IT BACK  and that was where
; the time went; Each lane of B is wanted THREE times  once in its own place
; and once by each of the two outputs below it in the row  so a flat chi makes
; seventy five journeys the length of the tape and seventy five more handing
; the lanes back; Measured  chi was ninety million instructions of which only
; twelve and a half million were the twenty five and64s and twenty five
; xor64s: EIGHTY SIX PER CENT WAS CARRYING;
;
; SO A ROW COMES DOWN TO A WORK BUFFER FIRST; A row of B is five lanes at one
; stride  which is forty CONSECUTIVE cells  so the whole of it moves in a single
; run of forty tokens and B is emptied as it goes; After that every one of the
; fifteen operand fetches for that row is a hop of a hundred cells or less  and
; only the five answers make the long journey down to A; Ten long journeys a row
; where there used to be thirty;
;
; THE SUM OF EVERY DISTANCE IN THIS FILE  counted as instructions per unit of
; byte value  came to 99200 for rho pi and chi together and comes to 45300;
; Measured end to end on a random state that is 118020255 instructions before
; and 64755239 after  which is forty five per cent off;
;
; AND B WAS DROPPED FROM CELL 400 TO CELL 328 at the same time  because the work
; buffer and the two frames are all that need to sit between A and B and they
; come to a hundred and twenty eight cells; That is worth 3600 of the 53900;
;
; Both halves were built and checked on their own before they were joined  each
; against a reference Keccak agreeing with SHA3 and SHAKE from a third party;
; Every distance below was worked out from the map above and written down;

; read the state little endian  leaving the pointer past it
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>
; ASSERT ptr=200
; ASSERT zero 200:547
; to the state  which is where rho and pi runs from
L200
; ASSERT ptr=0

; ==== rho and pi  PASTED rather than copied  so that the two files cannot ====
; ==== drift apart; it leaves its answer in B and the pointer back at nought ====
@@RHOPI@@ 0
; ASSERT ptr=0
; ASSERT zero 0:327
; ==== and now chi  over the array pi has just written ====
; Each ROW of B comes down to the work buffer in one run of forty  and every
; operand chi wants after that is a hop of a hundred cells or less; A row is
; forty cells at one stride  so one token moves the whole of it

; ==== row nought ====
R328
